{title: You Parents Hear What Jesus Taught}
{artist: Ludwig Helmbold · tr. William Martin Czamanske}
{key: F}
{time: 3/2}
{tempo: 125}

Verse 1
[F]You parents, hear [C]what Jesus taught When [F]little
ones to [C]him were brought: [F]Forbid them not, [C]but
heed my plea [A#]Permitting them to [F]come to me.

Verse 2
[C]Obey your Lord [F]and let his truth [A#]Be taught your
[C]children in their [F]youth That they [C]in church and
school [F]may dwell And [C]learn their Savior's [G]praise to tell.

Verse 3
For [C]if you love [F]them as you [A#]ought, To Christ [F]your
children will be [C]brought. If thus [Dm]you place them
[A#]in his care, [C]All in your family [F]well shall fare.
